window.DIGEST.foryou.push(...[{"id": "2112671236455014532", "url": "https://x.com/Rhoxbt/status/2112671236455014532", "text": "WHOEVER LEAKED THIS JEV KNOT SHOULD BE RUNNING TOPOLOGY\n\nI thought an agent loop meant a while-True with retries and a prayer that it exits.\n\nApparently not.\n\nThis knot's setup is much more interesting:\n\n→ INTAKE parses each packet from one of 3 lanes (email, chat, api) and tags it with an id, no raw text crosses past this node\n→ ROUTE sends the packet into one of 3 lobes of the trefoil, picked by jev.route() in a 12 line-per-second trace, no \"guess which lobe\"\n→ DECIDE runs noul and gate at the crossing with a 0.85 floor, PASS or RETRY, no silent escalation to the model\n→ ACT writes the draft or queues the call, 609 tokens per draft, every write logged against the packet id\n→ LOG closes the loop back to INTAKE for the next packet, flags 7 crossings whose over-under drifted from the trefoil invariant this hour\n\nso you get:\n\nPackets tagged. Lobes routed. Gates floored. Writes logged.\n\nthe interesting part isn't making the loop faster.\nit's giving every packet a closed route the state can't fall out of.\n\nInstead of a chain that collapses when any step fails, you run 10,082 decisions through a 3-crossing closed trefoil at $0.42, 207ms p50, 54% ACT and 27% IGNORE, and every packet exits where it entered.\n\nTag the packet. Route the lobe. Close the loop.", "name": "Rhoxbt", "handle": "Rhoxbt", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2101826030218424320/S_xejhcF_200x200.jpg", "likes": 23, "rts": 1, "replies": 3, "views": 1037, "ts": 1792535048, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112670664326881280/vid/avc1/720x900/7E6EoCGTblV2QmJ4.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112670664326881280/vid/avc1/1080x1350/3Fld0ydiC9g6slR4.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112670664326881280/img/HB5gp89SFRp9rLp_.jpg", "dur": 32}], "quote": {"id": "2100984487802708306", "url": "https://x.com/0xCodila/status/2100984487802708306", "text": "Jev is the \"Internet\" moment for the AI industry\n\nIt tells your agents and LLMs what to do next, in milliseconds and at almost zero cost\n\nIf you set it up correctly, you will have the AI engineer’s stack for 2028\n\nIn this article, I show you how https://x.com/i/article/2077744776565149697", "name": "codila", "handle": "0xCodila", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2064453666661441536/nj8n8Mei_200x200.jpg", "likes": 3485, "rts": 436, "replies": 94, "views": 2284715, "ts": 1789748710, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112645489703125319", "url": "https://x.com/AdamSchefter/status/2112645489703125319", "text": "Eagles’ roster moves:\n\n🏈Signed RB Elijah Mitchell to their practice squad.\n🏈Released C James Brockermeyer and RB Ian Wheeler from their practice squad.\n🏈Waived RB Jaydon Blue.\n🏈Waived/injured RB Carson Steele.", "name": "Adam Schefter", "handle": "AdamSchefter", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/793924061843914752/ycm8ibEE_200x200.jpg", "likes": 4824, "rts": 189, "replies": 115, "views": 1166075, "ts": 1792528910, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112575270498754648", "url": "https://x.com/RaghuRaghuram/status/2112575270498754648", "text": "We believe solving dexterous manipulation is one of the largest opportunities in robotics. Eka has built a Vision-Force-Action model that combines visual perception with force feedback from its robotic hands.\n\nVery excited to be partnering with @pulkitology, @haarnoja, and backing the @EkaRobotics team!", "name": "Raghu Raghuram", "handle": "RaghuRaghuram", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1399724601970671616/B4sklL4p_200x200.jpg", "likes": 37, "rts": 1, "replies": 2, "views": 3356, "ts": 1792512168, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112564529905221861", "url": "https://x.com/pulkitology/status/2112564529905221861", "text": "@EkaRobotics has raised a $150M Series A.\n\nGenerality v/s Performance is the fundamental tension at the frontier of robotics. Generality without performance is just a prototype. Performance without generality is just a single-purpose tool.\n\nCustomers shouldn’t have to choose. Eka breaks the tradeoff. Powered by our Vision-Force-Action (VFA) model, we deliver the performance and versatility customers need to put robots to work every day.\n\nEka is built on three convictions: \n⚡️Force is the language of manipulation. \n 🚀 Reinforcement learning is how dexterous manipulation scales. \n🎂 System 1—fast, reliable physical execution—is the bottleneck to solve.\n\nWith this funding, we will scale our model and accelerate customer deployments.\n\nGrateful to be building alongside a dream team and investors who share our ambition.", "name": "Pulkit Agrawal", "handle": "pulkitology", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/952619389857153025/Uhr_wfXH_200x200.jpg", "likes": 768, "rts": 81, "replies": 63, "views": 74233, "ts": 1792509608, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112558017560387585/vid/avc1/1280x720/DNbO508h66HSSQW0.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112558017560387585/vid/avc1/1920x1080/sFqUGJOXTFpyLjOs.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112558017560387585/img/dzODOZVG31Ix3Bko.jpg", "dur": 24}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112222848974537067", "url": "https://x.com/aimlapi/status/2112222848974537067", "text": "MiniMax M3.1 Flash mogs Muse and DeepSeek for FREE 🔥\n\nTry Space Bunny on https://aimlapi.com", "name": "AI/ML API", "handle": "aimlapi", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2061768103298473984/Zx3T3Ovp_200x200.jpg", "likes": 109, "rts": 5, "replies": 4, "views": 15518, "ts": 1792428145, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112221077640298497/vid/avc1/720x896/pbWPne5kl4RpA_qb.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112221077640298497/vid/avc1/1920x2392/N8nLqljAM-vC1Lak.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112221077640298497/img/d1c6AFtq37ArX4Uv.jpg", "dur": 25}], "quote": {"id": "2112150867868541221", "url": "https://x.com/MiniMax_AI/status/2112150867868541221", "text": "MiniMax M3.1 Flash: Space Performance + Bunny Speed\n\n🚀🐰 Yes, Space Bunny  - which has topped global leaderboards with 200T+ tokens - was an earlier version of M3.1 Flash.\n\n💰Redefining the performance economics of agentic AI. M3.1 Flash achieves frontier-level intelligence across key tasks such as Cowork (Automation-Bench: 62%; ALE: 30%), Coding (DeepSWE: 74%) and Visual Reasoning (BabyVision: 91%), at 1/3 the cost of M3 and 3x the speed.\n\nAPI pricing (flat rate): $0.15 / $0.60 per 1M input/output tokens, with cache reads at $0.015 / 1M tokens.\n\nModel weights will arrive on Oct 23.\n\nAPI: http://platform.minimax.io\nM Plan: https://www.minimax.io/m-plan\nMiniMax Code for desktop: https://agent.minimax.io/download", "name": "MiniMax (official)", "handle": "MiniMax_AI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1875100548535574529/VxHk9HyU_200x200.jpg", "likes": 7310, "rts": 656, "replies": 433, "views": 1165434, "ts": 1792410983, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HU_d5nbXEAAict2.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112260675112247712", "url": "https://x.com/le0xet/status/2112260675112247712", "text": "Holy f*ck, Opus 5.5 just replaced After Effects on my machine.\n\nIt's f*cking insane.\n\nNo plugin, no template pack, no tutorial. One PDF dropped into the chat and Opus 5.5 turns a brief into a rendered motion piece.\n\nThe PDF is a playbook for the model: brief -> storyboard -> assets -> scene code -> motion -> preview -> refine -> export. Every step written so Opus can run it without you touching a timeline.\n\nWhat came out on my first try: a 20 second product reel with typed intro, animated chart, 3D card flip and a clean export, built from a three-line brief and two reference frames.\n\nWant a new version? Change a color, a line of copy or the aspect ratio and render again. The animation lives in code, so nothing gets rebuilt by hand.\n\nDrop the PDF below into Opus 5.5 and see what it makes for you.\n\nThen read the full guide on motion design in the article below ↓", "name": "le0xet", "handle": "le0xet", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2104690774029840384/b8WG0cFJ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 107, "rts": 1, "replies": 4, "views": 5958, "ts": 1792437163, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112251401493520386/vid/avc1/1280x720/4KE_XMzc_dH4OoUd.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112251401493520386/vid/avc1/1922x1080/gcxbE__3mh-3e-Hr.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112251401493520386/img/ZwhjetDlJLP4KdTs.jpg", "dur": 12}], "quote": {"id": "2112249548991083005", "url": "https://x.com/slash1sol/status/2112249548991083005", "text": "A WORLD MODEL JUST DESIGNED A PHYSICAL OBJECT 100X FASTER AND 150X CHEAPER THAN GPT-6 ASTRA. DOWN TO THE SCREWS\n\n@skyfallai, the neolab from the deep learning pioneers behind Maluuba, just released SKY-001, the first engineering world model.\n\nText prompt or 2D sketch -> it dreams several designs in parallel -> picks the best -> breaks it into thousands of parts -> reassembles a CAD build that opens in Autodesk Fusion.\n\n• Why LLMs lose here\n> They produce 3D shapes that look right and cannot be built, no part hierarchy, no mechanical constraints, no feature tree.\n> Every design step burns tokens, and @spisallyouneed's team measured it: 100x faster and 150x cheaper than GPT-6 Astra on CAD and BIM.\n\n• Where this goes\n> Design is stage one, the goal is an AI general engineer running a company from design to production.\n> Their own org chart already reads 0 employees: an AI CEO, Sky 001 for design, Sky 001 for ops, plugged into AutoCAD, NetSuite, Salesforce and Zendesk.\n\nWorld models imagine and simulate before they act, LLMs guess one token at a time -> for autonomous manufacturing the first one wins.", "name": "slash1s", "handle": "slash1sol", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1979525426637672448/-H3r1kfe_200x200.jpg", "likes": 87, "rts": 4, "replies": 22, "views": 7772, "ts": 1792434510, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVA0XIYXMAA4EXY.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112302773827928334", "url": "https://x.com/GoogleCloudTech/status/2112302773827928334", "text": "Ever kick off an 8-hour agent job overnight, only to wake up to find it paused after 10 seconds because of a permission check?\n\nHear from @SmithaKolan and @lukeschlangen on why asynchronous human-in-the-loop continuity is a game changer for cloud agents → https://goo.gle/3WfnN4M", "name": "Google Cloud Tech", "handle": "GoogleCloudTech", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2047008659629391872/BfLTYOuh_200x200.jpg", "likes": 55, "rts": 5, "replies": 17, "views": 9126, "ts": 1792447200, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112264063010914304/vid/avc1/720x1280/EXatyO0mhQClMnXu.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112264063010914304/vid/avc1/1080x1920/at8Zopih8KRuoqw2.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVBE_-NWAAAIxSD.jpg", "dur": 33}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112599731641946408", "url": "https://x.com/Sourav_Bera_/status/2112599731641946408", "text": "Xiryn 0.5 is out.\n\nYour agents can now work on a schedule. Just tell one \"every weekday at 9, check new jobs for me\" and it does it, even with your browser closed.\n\nNo API key? One command sets up free local models.\n\n16 ready-made agents too.\n\nhttp://github.com/SouravBeraAkaSpeed/xiryn [ Drop a star ]\nhttp://xiryn.com", "name": "sourav bera", "handle": "Sourav_Bera_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2100146355536859136/fgoHhd6g_200x200.jpg", "likes": 17, "rts": 6, "replies": 2, "views": 2832, "ts": 1792518000, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112599272223133696/vid/avc1/720x720/STxDtnKPgJA9G_J2.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112599272223133696/vid/avc1/1080x1080/P73GB7PXEIZA_3Y6.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112599272223133696/img/2_CEyJmGrxYq-JCk.jpg", "dur": 55}], "quote": {"id": "2109675599090573762", "url": "https://x.com/Sourav_Bera_/status/2109675599090573762", "text": "Introducing Xiryn 🚀\n\nThe open-source personal agent that does everything Muse, Grok Bot and Dots do — on your own computer, without ever getting in your way.\n\ngithub :  https://github.com/SouravBeraAkaSpeed/xiryn\nweb : https://xiryn.com/", "name": "sourav bera", "handle": "Sourav_Bera_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2100146355536859136/fgoHhd6g_200x200.jpg", "likes": 584, "rts": 69, "replies": 31, "views": 275404, "ts": 1791820833, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2109675441846165504/vid/avc1/720x720/0me5Turn8_JPpbqt.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2109675441846165504/vid/avc1/1080x1080/w_RtC6VXXoszNDbN.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2109675441846165504/img/LpqMncPgIWILisPX.jpg", "dur": 67}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112635640302932408", "url": "https://x.com/Skaly__Bull/status/2112635640302932408", "text": "Most agents start every chat from scratch\nHermes Agent writes itself a skill instead\n\nFrom @NousResearch, free and MIT licensed\nAfter a hard task it saves the steps as a skill, then refines it\nOne gateway for Telegram, Discord, Slack and CLI, plus cron\n\nWhy @testdriveso should test it\n250K+ GitHub stars say people install it\nThe real question: is run 10 actually better than run 1?\n\nThe test I would run\nSame weekly report task, 10 runs, time and tokens per run\n\nRewarded TestDrive scouting", "name": "Skaly_Bull", "handle": "Skaly__Bull", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2020280527048126464/ANaDWHSB_200x200.jpg", "likes": 31, "rts": 0, "replies": 2, "views": 512, "ts": 1792526562, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112635496434196480/vid/avc1/1278x720/i1Ra2Q74BGZv_UCC.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112635496434196480/vid/avc1/1916x1078/_YQK5PE_jrSAkyZe.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112635496434196480/img/_P7zgZnFm9N10Idp.jpg", "dur": 23}], "quote": {"id": "2110066977612103909", "url": "https://x.com/testdriveso/status/2110066977612103909", "text": "TestDrive Tool Scouting 🔎\n\nFound a tool or a creator more builders should know about?\n\nSend them our way. If you find a tool or creator worth a test drive, we reward you for it.\n\nQuote-post this with your find 👇", "name": "Test Drive", "handle": "testdriveso", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2110091642866720768/Y-AXmtkW_200x200.jpg", "likes": 35, "rts": 8, "replies": 6, "views": 11716, "ts": 1791914145, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUh2rTAWUAApAAx.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112451593149067571", "url": "https://x.com/itsPolloAI/status/2112451593149067571", "text": "Think your city deserves its own movie? 🎬\n\nYou’ve still got until October 25 to enter Pollo AI’s One Minute Challenge and turn any U.S. city into a 60-second AI film.\n\nAn iPhone Duo is up for grabs, plus 10,000 credits each for 10 featured creators. Got a story worth telling? Now’s your chance! 👀\n\nMore information on Pollo AI, check the link in the comment!", "name": "Pollo AI", "handle": "itsPolloAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2108797484848066560/hUdK88SB_200x200.png", "likes": 35, "rts": 3, "replies": 10, "views": 3317, "ts": 1792482681, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2108436219982168270", "url": "https://x.com/itsPolloAI/status/2108436219982168270", "text": "A city. A million stories. You have one minute. 🎬  \n\nPollo AI’s global One Minute series kicks off with an in-person event in NYC on Oct 9, with more cities to come.  \n\nCan’t make it in person? Join the online challenge and turn a U.S. city into a one-minute film worth watching.   \n\nPrizes up for grabs: \n🥇 Grand Prize: iPhone Duo \n🏅 10 Featured Winners: 10,000 Credits each \n🎁 Plus membership rewards and more  \n\nSubmissions open Oct 9 and close Oct 25 at 11:59 PM EDT. Winners announced Nov 6.  \n\nYour city. Your story. One minute.  \n\nEnter the challenge in the comment!", "name": "Pollo AI", "handle": "itsPolloAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2108797484848066560/hUdK88SB_200x200.png", "likes": 46, "rts": 11, "replies": 20, "views": 13380, "ts": 1791525342, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2108435768666677248/vid/avc1/1280x720/l97hYYMPt-F3Yk-N.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2108435768666677248/vid/avc1/1920x1080/DV92JCmbMXOL_NRB.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2108435768666677248/img/Wze9y61eWj-lvXfO.jpg", "dur": 80}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112367031823839430", "url": "https://x.com/SAIRfoundation/status/2112367031823839430", "text": "Fields Medalists Terence Tao and Yu Deng discuss why understanding matters more than answers, how credit and citations hold up when machines build on centuries of human work, and why SAIR launched Open Math OS and Open Math Model. \n\nLearn more at https://openmathmodel.org.", "name": "SAIR", "handle": "SAIRfoundation", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2020783696870309888/-SEUG3_7_200x200.jpg", "likes": 52, "rts": 10, "replies": 1, "views": 43130, "ts": 1792462520, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112365978202091520/vid/avc1/640x360/6Z-iu__uOwc_VM3B.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112365978202091520/vid/avc1/1280x720/ZwJb9XHJdmwQQrpr.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112365978202091520/img/CACZJs9HSk-2owFi.jpg", "dur": 1366}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112723776999927811", "url": "https://x.com/0xSigil/status/2112723776999927811", "text": "Bringing more models on device- smaller and smarter @UnderdogAI 🐶", "name": "Sigil Wen", "handle": "0xSigil", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2101470722094989312/6BV11OZD_200x200.jpg", "likes": 14, "rts": 2, "replies": 3, "views": 1866, "ts": 1792547575, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112256989086859699", "url": "https://x.com/NVIDIARTXSpark/status/2112256989086859699", "text": "Love seeing what @UnderdogAI is bringing to RTX Spark. Their Saluki 27B model brings fast, private personal AI to your laptop in under 8GB of memory. 👏", "name": "NVIDIA RTX Spark", "handle": "NVIDIARTXSpark", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2061303426479431680/BDJQPK6Q_200x200.jpg", "likes": 131, "rts": 13, "replies": 3, "views": 11410, "ts": 1792436284, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112691096388276580", "url": "https://x.com/aaref/status/2112691096388276580", "text": "Listening to @ScottWu46, and his unique blend of EQ & IQ, you see how @cognition can bridge the different worlds of research lab & enterprise transformation company", "name": "Aaref Hilaly", "handle": "aaref", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1309522729591160833/vyqvT4tj_200x200.jpg", "likes": 17, "rts": 4, "replies": 0, "views": 4360, "ts": 1792539783, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112594042236387418", "url": "https://x.com/BainCapVC/status/2112594042236387418", "text": "“Remember Devin? It works now.”\n\nAfter the internet said it wouldn’t, Cognition put that on a billboard.\n\nThe @cognition story with @ScottWu46 and @aaref.", "name": "Bain Capital Ventures", "handle": "BainCapVC", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1790404088833728512/HShSGp-k_200x200.jpg", "likes": 162, "rts": 14, "replies": 3, "views": 22282, "ts": 1792516644, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112591615202361344/vid/avc1/1280x720/qGyzic7a9tvejRl-.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112591615202361344/vid/avc1/1920x1080/tlFvVZr39fvPaLr7.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112591615202361344/img/g0dDUWezH7mBnsph.jpg", "dur": 365}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Research & Safety", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112605646998716684", "url": "https://x.com/ProbyShandilya/status/2112605646998716684", "text": "Some other examples of great investments at valuations that seemed high in the moment (relative to revenue):  \n - @mamoonha did the Figma Series B at $115M post at 500K ARR \n- @andrew__reed did the Figma Series C at $400M post at 4M ARR \n- @andrew__reed also did Vanta Series A $480M post at 10M ARR (going 2 to 10) \n- Altimeter did the Snowflake Series C (a 45M round) at 2M ARR  \n\nFew things worth saying here:  \n\n- there are no \"one-size-fits-all\" rules or frameworks when it comes to revenue/valuation....every company is so unique and on their own journey. have to underwrite each company differently\n - there are other great ways to quantify momentum outside of pure revenue. for example Vanta had 3.5M net new ARR in the quarter before the A. \n- how Altimeter built conviction on Snowflake was very interesting. they downloaded the product and used it / saw it's differentiation against other OLAP alternatives firsthand", "name": "Proby Shandilya", "handle": "ProbyShandilya", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1958555379454951424/m8DQwdPR_200x200.jpg", "likes": 39, "rts": 0, "replies": 0, "views": 6629, "ts": 1792519411, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112579848149639489", "url": "https://x.com/HarryStebbings/status/2112579848149639489", "text": "Why price does not matter in a world of AI and the metric that truly determines value\n\n“When we invested in Abridge, they were at $5M of ARR, and we were paying a $700M to $800M valuation.\n\nWhen we invested in Anthropic in that $15BN round, I think they were at $100M. Lagora was at $20M of ARR when we led that $1.8BN round.\n\nWhat I care about is the NTM basis. What do I think in the next 12 months this thing can be, and do I feel like this is a reasonable multiple in the next 12 months?” @spdholakia\n\nLove to hear your thoughts @loganbartlett @jaltma @GavinSBaker @afc @poyark", "name": "Harry Stebbings", "handle": "HarryStebbings", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1862557919717265409/2xIkJF_g_200x200.jpg", "likes": 36, "rts": 4, "replies": 17, "views": 19006, "ts": 1792513260, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112217498699333632/vid/avc1/1280x720/IrwTk4LFApjzsSh_.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112217498699333632/vid/avc1/1920x1080/HKq9IJMJA4dt6mSN.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112217498699333632/img/QoSwUt_ODp15R3ye.jpg", "dur": 45}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112246638714683557", "url": "https://x.com/HarshithLucky3/status/2112246638714683557", "text": "Fable 5.5 is coming....", "name": "Harshith", "handle": "HarshithLucky3", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1940482570484858880/dYD7sVKE_200x200.jpg", "likes": 112, "rts": 0, "replies": 4, "views": 3069, "ts": 1792433816, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112212326795362560", "url": "https://x.com/theinformation/status/2112212326795362560", "text": "Anthropic is preparing a new AI model that can better infer what users are trying to accomplish, even when their instructions are vague. \n\nThe unreleased model also shows stronger reasoning and more creative problem-solving abilities, according to a person who has used it.\n\nFull story: https://thein.fo/4irv4XQ", "name": "The Information", "handle": "theinformation", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1747484907163516928/d_K3Z_hH_200x200.jpg", "likes": 488, "rts": 38, "replies": 17, "views": 113587, "ts": 1792425636, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.05, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112568596291551416", "url": "https://x.com/DynamicWebPaige/status/2112568596291551416", "text": "Looking at the stats at the top of the frame:\n\n⚡ 20 mins vs. 12h 16m\n💸 ~$1.13 vs. $114.34\n\nPushing the Pareto frontier on speed and cost is what makes agentic workflows actually viable in production. And the money you save could buy an *actual* mechanical keyboard! 🤣", "name": "👩‍💻 Paige Bailey", "handle": "DynamicWebPaige", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/626762747330457600/X3Bx503W_200x200.jpg", "likes": 35, "rts": 0, "replies": 4, "views": 4134, "ts": 1792510577, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112507253391561075", "url": "https://x.com/AIMind_Ai/status/2112507253391561075", "text": "$114 for a honey keyboard, and Claude Opus 5.5 needed three tries to get it right.\n\nWhat the f*ck. I could've bought a real one at the store and still had money left for honey.\n\nGemini 4 Argon did it for about a dollar, 102x cheaper.\n\nWhich one would you put on your desk?", "name": "AiMind", "handle": "AIMind_Ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2076746901974618112/HW4ZZGT9_200x200.jpg", "likes": 76, "rts": 7, "replies": 11, "views": 16408, "ts": 1792495952, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112507037846224896/vid/avc1/720x900/t9GqcD7Z8_P1pItI.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112507037846224896/vid/avc1/1080x1350/q8MF74DMppeoeOJ6.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112507037846224896/img/weL7nLC8F3UB0phB.jpg", "dur": 33}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.05, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112611452771250666", "url": "https://x.com/_Chain_Duck_/status/2112611452771250666", "text": "Smart TV full of ads? People are now handing it to an AI agent\n\nOne dev says Claude Code stripped 25 bloat packages off a Xiaomi TV. His prompt was reportedly copied by a few thousand people in 2 days (his claim)\n\nRisk is real: one user bricked an Android TV", "name": "ChainDuck", "handle": "_Chain_Duck_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2056832148875706368/I7Ykt1Ac_200x200.jpg", "likes": 15, "rts": 0, "replies": 11, "views": 478, "ts": 1792520795, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112611426254630912/vid/avc1/720x906/IF4wRTmHEztoulsD.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112611426254630912/vid/avc1/1080x1360/2Z8UbonxYTRrFVEV.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112611426254630912/img/CJMe_2fA--8Dqnde.jpg", "dur": 14}], "quote": {"id": "2111877678823342470", "url": "https://x.com/_Chain_Duck_/status/2111877678823342470", "text": "https://x.com/i/article/2111874521305075712", "name": "ChainDuck", "handle": "_Chain_Duck_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2056832148875706368/I7Ykt1Ac_200x200.jpg", "likes": 20, "rts": 0, "replies": 1, "views": 2136, "ts": 1792345850, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.05, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112631749717180691", "url": "https://x.com/feeldotcash/status/2112631749717180691", "text": "Anthropic was valued at $965B in May.\n\nReports have put its potential IPO valuation as high as $2T.\n\nGet exposure before it goes public.\n\nTap. Done.\n\nhttps://feel.cash/stocks/anthropic", "name": "Feel.cash", "handle": "feeldotcash", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2090009813426077696/-P_b4T8v_200x200.jpg", "likes": 18, "rts": 5, "replies": 1, "views": 1330, "ts": 1792525634, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112631280630104064/vid/avc1/1370x720/8zYA-JprxmIPZXfa.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112631280630104064/vid/avc1/2560x1344/mLx4CPIz0e-S_KnY.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112631280630104064/img/VuSa82w8Q9AnDZAv.jpg", "dur": 8}], "quote": {"id": "2112249206748373306", "url": "https://x.com/FT/status/2112249206748373306", "text": "Anthropic’s planned IPO could be the biggest stock market debut in history. What does it mean for investors, AI and the tech industry as a whole? Our reporters will answer your questions: https://ft.trib.al/OAzDhvM", "name": "Financial Times", "handle": "FT", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/931156393108885504/EqEMtLhM_200x200.jpg", "likes": 104, "rts": 16, "replies": 13, "views": 27672, "ts": 1792434429, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVA3dBzXwAAAcDU.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.05, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112673946466476234", "url": "https://x.com/0xDevShah/status/2112673946466476234", "text": "if everyone had infinite tokens and infinite tokens/sec, i think everyone would be a researcher. curiosity and discovery are deeply human. it's just that most people don't have the patience, time, or resources to spend years chasing a question. but what if they didn't have to wait years?\n\nnext year, we'll run today's frontier models on consumer GPUs. in 2 years, we'll have AGI in a zip file.\n\nimagine billions of people suddenly have the ability to pursue their curiosity and make discoveries. when everyone can be a researcher, they'll need a research lab. this is ArkenOS!", "name": "Dev Shah", "handle": "0xDevShah", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1859072760938721280/eihad2RU_200x200.jpg", "likes": 15, "rts": 3, "replies": 3, "views": 766, "ts": 1792535695, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112032537652650022", "url": "https://x.com/0xDevShah/status/2112032537652650022", "text": "Introducing Optimus-1, the first swarm harness for autonomous research. Generally available in ArkenOS, starting now.\n\nOptimus-1 lets ArkenOS spawn a swarm that runs the entire discovery loop on hard research problems autonomously. The harness samples the hypothesis space in parallel and works the tails of the distribution, chasing every anomaly until it resolves into an artifact or a discovery. We want every researcher to have a lab of their own, and to see how far their curiosity can go.\n\nUnlike coding agents, Optimus-1 is designed for long-horizon discovery, where most branches fail, and the hard part is knowing which result to believe. It keeps what replicates and keeps pushing past the edge of what's known.\n\nWe're still early, but ArkenOS is helping hundreds of teams, from RL environments and data labs to frontier research groups, scale the alpha in their core research.\n\nIf you're working on a hard research problem and want to try it, my DMs are open. I'd love to hear what you'd point it at.", "name": "Dev Shah", "handle": "0xDevShah", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1859072760938721280/eihad2RU_200x200.jpg", "likes": 664, "rts": 72, "replies": 41, "views": 37409, "ts": 1792382771, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112032208794103808/vid/avc1/1280x720/WGxACKktRuHfa15I.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112032208794103808/vid/avc1/3840x2160/sC_hWcSCQFtGpQcN.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112032208794103808/img/J0h7jYI_BWxBTwUz.jpg", "dur": 56}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.05, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112575874650542214", "url": "https://x.com/urdeaintech/status/2112575874650542214", "text": "Voxel is a home robot built around the small things.\n\n→ Resets the house after a mess\n→ Finds your phone or wallet\n→ Fetches what you need\n\nThat's where a home robot starts to make sense", "name": "Samuel Urdea", "handle": "urdeaintech", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2092899894218416128/ZypwJ5s7_200x200.jpg", "likes": 31, "rts": 3, "replies": 1, "views": 651, "ts": 1792512312, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112565146354860151", "url": "https://x.com/make_robot_go/status/2112565146354860151", "text": "Introducing Voxel, a droid butler made by Tuesday Labs.", "name": "Ros Shinkle", "handle": "make_robot_go", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1761551110303825920/JvPQiGQd_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2181, "rts": 228, "replies": 203, "views": 1850860, "ts": 1792509755, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/960x720/cMYjra9bu_jYUTYR.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/2880x2160/glhkyiQ6K97Rmq93.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112564839251931136/img/GKLfsqVaQmO0B-kn.jpg", "dur": 89}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.05, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112378276681580942", "url": "https://x.com/WayOfMenn/status/2112378276681580942", "text": "Jensen Huang on The smartest person he's ever met:", "name": "Way of Men", "handle": "WayOfMenn", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2062051683539271680/67GXnHBz_200x200.jpg", "likes": 9215, "rts": 957, "replies": 182, "views": 983985, "ts": 1792465201, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111366694308655104/vid/avc1/540x360/zFf7M_E6RMtJS6NN.mp4?tag=14", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111366694308655104/vid/avc1/720x480/FQE6Wp-064EgVEi1.mp4?tag=14", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2111366694308655104/img/YQ97JjsLajU8-L1c.jpg", "dur": 124}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112204695456616829", "url": "https://x.com/AskPerplexity/status/2112204695456616829", "text": "Computer built an interactive Lord of the Rings map that tracks the journeys of the main characters across Middle-earth, chapter by chapter.\n\nIt built the map from scratch by placing 179 locations, 41 rivers, and 23 roads, baked the ranges into a heightfield, inked the relief in a GLSL shader, and plotted 537 journey legs.\n\nTry it: http://middle-earth.pplx.app", "name": "Computer", "handle": "AskPerplexity", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2028889294174380032/1hOF3gRi_200x200.jpg", "likes": 103, "rts": 4, "replies": 9, "views": 12048, "ts": 1792423816, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112204636115574784/vid/avc1/1280x720/9YJGMOh72xnnpuSj.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112204636115574784/vid/avc1/1920x1080/q5SfnCqg18XDuEq6.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112204636115574784/img/mE_MHCFp0zRCV3v9.jpg", "dur": 97}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112522086014972238", "url": "https://x.com/borrhensaidi/status/2112522086014972238", "text": "We’re giving away 5+ Claude Max annual subscriptions. Yes, ANNUAL. 👀\n\nSwarmPane builds, ships, and gives back. This is just the beginning. Join the swarm. More surprises incoming.\n\nhttps://swarmpane.com/", "name": "borhen saidi", "handle": "borrhensaidi", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2085022334029533184/fvWmeUEb_200x200.jpg", "likes": 38, "rts": 0, "replies": 5, "views": 16605, "ts": 1792499488, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112522036895494144/vid/avc1/1382x720/cvwtfi-V-UFqVel2.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112522036895494144/vid/avc1/1920x1000/2KtoNKRse1i9rJ9z.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112522036895494144/img/YFgKLz5OehRyOPn8.jpg", "dur": 12}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112604762289946819", "url": "https://x.com/lovart_ai/status/2112604762289946819", "text": "Off-brand details, caught before you deliver.\n\nCanvas Check-up: Arti flags what doesn't match your brand on the canvas, and you fix it in one click.\n\nArti, your first personal design agent, has memory and takes initiative. Now in Lovart 2.0.\n\n#BuiltWithLovart", "name": "Lovart AI", "handle": "lovart_ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2065372538763694080/KSuXj3OU_200x200.jpg", "likes": 27, "rts": 2, "replies": 2, "views": 1256, "ts": 1792519200, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112591903351062528/vid/avc1/1280x720/6DYZadWGFg2I4Dbg.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112591903351062528/vid/avc1/1920x1080/l3N0oP3Zh0xs1dW_.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFytYLX0AA-ztl.jpg", "dur": 17}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112574729575932075", "url": "https://x.com/thisiskp_/status/2112574729575932075", "text": "\"The next leap in AI coding won't come from OpenAI or Anthropic.\" Big bet with a $5.5M seed behind it..\n\nBut they're right about one thing. Your sessions are the most valuable training data you own, and right now they just disappear.\n\nHyped to see this one open source 💪", "name": "KP", "handle": "thisiskp_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1288449070344937473/fKlvccnM_200x200.jpg", "likes": 20, "rts": 3, "replies": 6, "views": 3073, "ts": 1792512039, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112552451547001218", "url": "https://x.com/jqdsouza/status/2112552451547001218", "text": "We’re betting our $5.5M seed round that the next leap in AI coding won’t come from OpenAI or Anthropic.\n\nIt’ll come from a new feedback loop that learns from you.\n\nIntroducing Beacon: open-source, self-improving memory for coding agents.\n\nYour sessions capture how you debug and solve problems. Today, that context gets lost and you have to re-explain things every time you switch tools.\n\nBeacon continuously distills your sessions into reusable skills across Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, and 20+ harnesses, so your next agent can learn from the last.\n\nBeacon is free and OSS 🌟 http://github.com/Asymptote-Labs/agent-beacon\n\nWhy should the frontier labs be the only ones winning with your sessions?\n\nYou already did the work. Now let your coding agents learn from you.", "name": "Justin D'Souza", "handle": "jqdsouza", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1817440734766604288/99FuIxoo_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1279, "rts": 141, "replies": 251, "views": 425746, "ts": 1792506728, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112552129952874496/vid/avc1/1280x720/mhJ2imMl6mA4kQEF.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112552129952874496/vid/avc1/1920x1080/2nvostHi1eUMqE7-.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112552129952874496/img/X1ifILIq6yhlSaGJ.jpg", "dur": 109}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112343898391552235", "url": "https://x.com/PyTorch/status/2112343898391552235", "text": "#PyTorchCon North America 2026 starts tomorrow in San Jose, bringing the open source AI community together to accelerate open intelligence.\n\nAcross PyTorch, @vllm_project, @DeepSpeedAI, @raydistributed, Helion, and Safetensors, our program explores the full AI stack, from bare metal infrastructure to applications and agent-based systems, through technical talks, hands-on workshops, and candid conversations.\n\nTomorrow and Wednesday, October 20–21, the program spans seven tracks: Applications, Core PyTorch, Inference, Introduction, Kernel Engineering, Responsible AI, and Training.\n\nKeynote speakers include @sparkycollier (PyTorch Foundation); @cmazzaanthony (@Shopify); @albanDesmaison, Edward Yang, Jana van Greunen, and Zongwei Zhou (@Meta); @clattner_llvm (@Qualcomm); @istoica05 (@UCBerkeley / @anyscalecompute); Robert Hundt (@amazon); @sarahookr (@adaption_ai); @simon_mo_ (@inferact); Carlos Costa and Priya Nagpurkar (@IBM); Abdullah Gharaibeh and Bill Jia (@googlecloud); Stephen Watt (@RedHat); Ujval Kapasi (@nvidia); Mazin Gilbert (@AgenticAIFdn); Zhipeng Wang (@Google); Rachad Alao (@cohere); Yiwei Song (@CrusoeAI); and @marksaroufim (Core Automation).\n\nBeyond the talks, exchange ideas in Birds of a Feather discussions, ask questions in Meet the Developers sessions, and watch sponsor presentations in the Demo Theater.\n\nTuesday offers more opportunities for conversation: discuss presenters’ work at the evening poster session, connect at the Women & Non-Binary in PyTorch Lunch, or meet Inference Engineering author Philip Kiely at his book signing.\n\nExplore the program: https://events.linuxfoundation.org/pytorch-conference-north-america/program/schedule/\n\nJoin us at #PyTorchCon tomorrow and Wednesday: https://events.linuxfoundation.org/pytorch-conference-north-america/register/", "name": "PyTorch", "handle": "PyTorch", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1813965160702451712/yXV1vRhr_200x200.jpg", "likes": 44, "rts": 7, "replies": 11, "views": 7422, "ts": 1792457005, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVCNlLjXUAAkK8Y.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112464345728721085", "url": "https://x.com/_ScottCondron/status/2112464345728721085", "text": "Auto-research on idle GPU capacity\n\nEvery idle GPU is spice that isn't flowing. \nAnd the spice must flow.\n\nOne idea to keep your GPUs busy is an auto-research pipeline: a queue of different ideas for agents to try whenever the GPUs are not doing higher priority work.\n\nOn @CoreWeave you can build this from: \n\n- SUNK (Slurm on Kubernetes) to share nodes between priority jobs and agents, with preemption so priority work gets done - GPU sandboxes to run agent-written code in isolation - Spot capacity for cheap extra capacity  - Dedicated inference plus Dynamo agent_hints to rank the agents' own model calls below production traffic\n\nAnd you can see what the agents are doing: traces, evals and training runs in one place.", "name": "Scott Condron", "handle": "_ScottCondron", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1016982898556141569/R09dBwgv_200x200.jpg", "likes": 48, "rts": 2, "replies": 2, "views": 2750, "ts": 1792485722, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112464308453924864/vid/avc1/720x720/pW9WQVZRl-fcUVOL.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112464308453924864/vid/avc1/1440x1440/G3BVENQIR5e4PcZg.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112464308453924864/img/ZYcl0RY_pynkIWqf.jpg", "dur": 12}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112671510913482822", "url": "https://x.com/BBCWorld/status/2112671510913482822", "text": "Alberta's decisive decision to stay in Canada gives Carney backing to take on Trump https://bbc.in/4sdvfcC", "name": "BBC News (World)", "handle": "BBCWorld", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1529107170448523264/q3VwEx38_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2132, "rts": 331, "replies": 861, "views": 345930, "ts": 1792535114, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Politics & World", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112628249096593513", "url": "https://x.com/AnnLLarson/status/2112628249096593513", "text": "holy fucking shit", "name": "Ann Larson", "handle": "AnnLLarson", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2098946083712094208/H_vIW-A__200x200.jpg", "likes": 4485, "rts": 344, "replies": 18, "views": 320260, "ts": 1792524799, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112604932797026411", "url": "https://x.com/william_fitz/status/2112604932797026411", "text": "\"Speculative data center debt is being repackaged and sold to pension and retirement funds, university endowments, and other institutional investors in a manner eerily reminiscent of the subprime bubble.\"\n\nhttps://ourfinancialsecurity.org/resources/brace-for-impact-protecting-people-and-the-economy-when-the-ai-bubble-bursts/", "name": "William Fitzgerald", "handle": "william_fitz", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1868743858303254530/Fg_1fdZb_200x200.jpg", "likes": 4910, "rts": 1131, "replies": 84, "views": 704974, "ts": 1792519240, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112641692998533269", "url": "https://x.com/kushalbyatnal/status/2112641692998533269", "text": "I don't think people realize how good AI-generated documents have gotten\n\nwe built a game so you can see for yourself\n\nsome documents are real, others are fake. can you tell the difference?\n\nhttps://www.extend.ai/fraud-arcade", "name": "Kushal Byatnal", "handle": "kushalbyatnal", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1225315201311854592/GHIT4gYq_200x200.jpg", "likes": 23, "rts": 2, "replies": 2, "views": 1523, "ts": 1792528005, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112639960558002176/vid/avc1/1280x720/4N3jQm1i-cvEiWuj.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112639960558002176/vid/avc1/1920x1080/NtFVVO5R1hCQqP8R.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112639960558002176/img/d6MuSZfPpH4R9SIb.jpg", "dur": 57}], "quote": {"id": "2112221199560536193", "url": "https://x.com/kushalbyatnal/status/2112221199560536193", "text": "AI-generated fake documents grew 500% last year, and humans can no longer tell the difference\n\nThat's why we’re launching Extend Verify, the first document fraud detection API built for agents\n\nVerify catches the fastest growing types of document fraud, including:\n\n- fully AI-generated documents\n- localized AI edits (down to a single modified character)\n- patched text, overlays, and in-painting from Photoshop, PDF editors, and coding agents\n- digital tampering after a document was signed\n- and many more\n\nIn our internal evals, Verify detected over 96% of AI-generated and tampered documents.\n\nVerify is available today: https://www.extend.ai/verify/request-access", "name": "Kushal Byatnal", "handle": "kushalbyatnal", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1225315201311854592/GHIT4gYq_200x200.jpg", "likes": 191, "rts": 20, "replies": 52, "views": 25179, "ts": 1792427751, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112220772509126659/vid/avc1/1280x720/oKPir6JnEhWZ9Sb6.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112220772509126659/vid/avc1/3840x2160/faX5ymXCJHzNZQlR.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112220772509126659/img/ydg4Gnovrkk91TCy.jpg", "dur": 100}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112722931729981719", "url": "https://x.com/boneGPT/status/2112722931729981719", "text": "the slopcannon loves you\nthank you", "name": "bone", "handle": "boneGPT", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2006021278281478144/veZLsQq9_200x200.jpg", "likes": 20, "rts": 1, "replies": 1, "views": 758, "ts": 1792547374, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112691725286224200", "url": "https://x.com/HeyoPatriot/status/2112691725286224200", "text": "Heyoo, shoutout to the SlopCannon devs and all the wiggas in the group chat, 🐷🎤 Just wanted to say Thank You.  I lurk more than I post, but your nonstop builds, unhinged experiments, and pure love for acceleration pulled me off the sidelines.\n\nmy app drops tonight 👽⚡️ drinks are on me 🍺🇺🇸", "name": "heyopatriot", "handle": "HeyoPatriot", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1958631581603471360/BYhAar5X_200x200.jpg", "likes": 15, "rts": 3, "replies": 3, "views": 750, "ts": 1792539933, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112691617010188289/vid/avc1/1280x720/XyIy5o29qsDpuTAX.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112691617010188289/vid/avc1/2560x1440/Ns47VGVpMWjPu90d.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112691617010188289/img/bNsTKxQlg3of87FC.jpg", "dur": 113}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112724875874025642", "url": "https://x.com/atulkumarzz/status/2112724875874025642", "text": "Imagine asking your agent who won the game and getting the answer instantly, with the right source to back it up.\n\nThat’s what @youdotcom is bringing with Sportradar. No digging around for scores, no telling your agent where to look. Just ask and get the answer.", "name": "Atul Kumar", "handle": "atulkumarzz", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1602322477501140992/BJSVHwBm_200x200.jpg", "likes": 7, "rts": 6, "replies": 0, "views": 563, "ts": 1792547837, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112631743564165401", "url": "https://x.com/youdotcom/status/2112631743564165401", "text": "Who won the 49ers game last night? 🏈\n\nYour AI agent should already know.\n\nWith @youdotcom 's live answers powered by Sportradar, get real-time sports scores and answers backed by the right source, without having to tell your agent where to look.\n\nTry it for free - https://you.com/platform/playground/web-search?knowledge=core&query=Who+won+the+49ers+game+yesterday%3F%0A", "name": "You.com", "handle": "youdotcom", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1814006937194795008/LW6Ol2Q1_200x200.png", "likes": 6, "rts": 0, "replies": 0, "views": 851, "ts": 1792525633, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112627741883592706/vid/avc1/720x720/ytGO4yFQXqPypWnA.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112627741883592706/vid/avc1/2160x2160/kZ3oOIm2PTsyla8O.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112627741883592706/img/XVwsD0GWOrpjfDGt.jpg", "dur": 8}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112529374855692473", "url": "https://x.com/val_soonafter/status/2112529374855692473", "text": "I never worked with 3D before. Lately, Opus is changing what I thought my limits were.\n\nAI can produce a lot of slop, very efficiently! Poor guidance sets the machine on autopilot.\n\nBUT it can also get you to places you would’ve never gotten by yourself.", "name": "Val Guerra", "handle": "val_soonafter", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2102463117691338752/-vReGzmb_200x200.jpg", "likes": 41, "rts": 0, "replies": 3, "views": 1527, "ts": 1792501226, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112529286217568256/vid/avc1/1280x720/cIDMkFf0ZG4Kng00.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112529286217568256/vid/avc1/1920x1080/PNPx-WcK1aMEeeBl.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112529286217568256/img/HKdEw57st49Ipz5g.jpg", "dur": 7}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112691844358262973", "url": "https://x.com/CNN/status/2112691844358262973", "text": "Several Trump administration officials, advisers and close allies describe a toxic mix of jockeying for power and preemptive finger-pointing ahead of the midterms.\n\n\"It's more brutal than any other situation in modern times in the White House,\" said one Trump ally. \"You can't trust anybody here.\" https://cnn.it/4zKoeTc", "name": "CNN", "handle": "CNN", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1669780523911110656/K9gaaM1g_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1873, "rts": 505, "replies": 586, "views": 743588, "ts": 1792539962, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Politics & World", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2111838943016833235", "url": "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2111838943016833235", "text": "The new Tesla Roadster accelerates faster than a fighter jet taking off from an aircraft carrier", "name": "Elon Musk", "handle": "elonmusk", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2103567689515954176/aR-Kjpp4_200x200.jpg", "likes": 44673, "rts": 5093, "replies": 3498, "views": 2943609, "ts": 1792336614, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2111730102618972636", "url": "https://x.com/XFreeze/status/2111730102618972636", "text": "The new Tesla Roadster produces more thrust than an F-16 fighter jet at military power\n\nRoadster Thrust augment:\n>80 kN (~18,000 lbf)\n\nF-16 with F100-PW-229:\n~79.2 kN (~17,800 lbf) without afterburner\n\nTesla packed enough cold-gas thrust into a car that exceeds the non-afterburning thrust of an F-16 engine\n\nWith afterburner, the F-16 exceeds at ~130 kN\n\nBut the fact this comparison even exists is insane\n\nTesla just pushed automotive engineering deep into aerospace territory", "name": "X Freeze", "handle": "XFreeze", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1876785200010539008/2_HFJjq9_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2734, "rts": 345, "replies": 193, "views": 2019648, "ts": 1792310665, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111730001943154688/vid/avc1/720x720/z4yJK-E034o81MTG.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111730001943154688/vid/avc1/2160x2160/Qnfp2Y_plZivkL8I.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2111730001943154688/img/VO4c1JTFmkAQUGSO.jpg", "dur": 18}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.03, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112265788963110920", "url": "https://x.com/runable_hq/status/2112265788963110920", "text": "FLUX.3 Max is seriously amazing 🔥\n\nSide by side with Seedance 2.5, \nthe quality is surprisingly close.\n\n→ 22× faster in my test\n→ ~5× cheaper at comparable 720p pricing on Layer\n→ Native audio\n→ Up to 20-second videos\n\nThe speed difference is WILD.", "name": "Runable", "handle": "runable_hq", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2091784345648336896/ppDHg8vE_200x200.jpg", "likes": 69, "rts": 6, "replies": 10, "views": 12722, "ts": 1792438382, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112264811316916224/vid/avc1/1280x720/SVNnTQjR1J2LYZ5H.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112264811316916224/vid/avc1/1920x1080/fq8tYdWtUBgzbXBD.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112264811316916224/img/3mFUO8V2WlufpDTH.jpg", "dur": 20}], "quote": {"id": "2112255353677328415", "url": "https://x.com/bfl_ai/status/2112255353677328415", "text": "Introducing FLUX 3 Max.\n\nFastest in the west. Fast enough to try anything. And everything.\n\nGenerate a 10-second video in 12 seconds.\n\nTied for #1 in image-to-video. 22× faster than Seedance 2.5 at the same quality.\n\nFLUX 3 is a model designed for customization. @fal adapted and optimized it to create FLUX 3 Max.", "name": "Black Forest Labs", "handle": "bfl_ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1954888731053142016/NDyG-4-j_200x200.jpg", "likes": 955, "rts": 106, "replies": 91, "views": 65906, "ts": 1792435894, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112238793139044352/vid/avc1/720x720/6c2tLuZIRfEMaRz7.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112238793139044352/vid/avc1/2160x2160/5hWxA_d-ViViLNG2.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112238793139044352/img/1Uf4xVFGip9CN4_K.jpg", "dur": 15}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.03, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112483780187320684", "url": "https://x.com/SkyNews/status/2112483780187320684", "text": "BREAKING: Multiple online services are down or 'experiencing issues.'\n \nGoogle Cloud has reported \"issues\" in its western Europe region affecting dozens of websites, including; Revolut, Royal Mail and HSBC.\n \nLatest updates ➡️ https://trib.al/M16q5UZ\n\n📺 Sky 501", "name": "Sky News", "handle": "SkyNews", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1604907328242962433/P_79at43_200x200.jpg", "likes": 3452, "rts": 1547, "replies": 233, "views": 1441649, "ts": 1792490355, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112483638566629376/vid/avc1/1280x720/x1PxUU10fYoB3AzR.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112483638566629376/vid/avc1/1920x1080/lSZuJN5mJdRJiIO2.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVEMvlaXsAEzmhd.jpg", "dur": 128}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.03, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112458848971952580", "url": "https://x.com/AiHubMix/status/2112458848971952580", "text": "MiniMax M3.1 Flash is kind of ridiculous at 3D frontend\n\n$1.62 for an entire autumn valley\n\nBuilding a scene like this used to mean:\n> hiring a 3D artist\n> modeling, texturing, lighting, one step at a time\n> setting up an engine just to walk around in it\n> and often ending up with a single still render\n\nAmberbrook, today:\n> one prompt\n> a stone watermill, its wheel slowly turning\n> a stream running under a stone arch bridge into a pond\n> an ivy-covered woodcutter's hut tucked at the edge of the woods\n> runs in a browser tab: drag, zoom, pan, or hit Tour and the camera flies you through 5 stops\n\nThe details are what got me\n\nSmoke drifting from the chimney, warm light in the windows, the whole mill reflected in the pond\nAnd an axe still stuck in a tree stump\n\nTry MiniMax M3.1 Flash on AIHubMix: https://aihubmix.com", "name": "AIHubmix", "handle": "AiHubMix", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2005111189165236224/QuN045cN_200x200.jpg", "likes": 36, "rts": 4, "replies": 5, "views": 2919, "ts": 1792484411, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112455834781487104/vid/avc1/1280x720/IvCteWT6tbi4tyI5.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112455834781487104/vid/avc1/2560x1440/v_M8d5Z-AM_BlkTR.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112455834781487104/img/pTwu_6y1iYPIjLxJ.jpg", "dur": 31}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.03, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112612481826979846", "url": "https://x.com/harleyfoote_/status/2112612481826979846", "text": "Software IP died last week.\n\nNot gradually. Not eventually. Headless agents just made the entire business model evaporate.\n▶ Full video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xIFMwhvvUUo — via The AI Daily Brief: Artificial Intelligence News", "name": "Harley Lewis Foote", "handle": "harleyfoote_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2080658812382449664/VF5NORY-_200x200.jpg", "likes": 31, "rts": 0, "replies": 2, "views": 519, "ts": 1792521040, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112612424792604672/vid/avc1/640x360/bffn4bfTGL7Aqvse.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112612424792604672/vid/avc1/1280x720/FZKGkiam570myU4V.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112612424792604672/img/BQYGkfWWxJqyhFCw.jpg", "dur": 45}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.03, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112605757975966149", "url": "https://x.com/Arj_786/status/2112605757975966149", "text": "Open-source OCR has a new leader: OXR\n\n🔹 olmOCR-Bench · OmniDocBench · DocParsingBench winner\n🔹 Speed champ, single RTX PRO 6000\n🔹 1.7x LightOnOCR-2-1B\n\nFormulas + tables. Swap the layout model. RSI + parallel ordering inside.\n\n👉 https://github.com/SoMarkAI/OXR", "name": "Aria Arooj", "handle": "Arj_786", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2023131891621339136/xHIj4IXT_200x200.jpg", "likes": 6, "rts": 6, "replies": 6, "views": 191, "ts": 1792519437, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112574994152636502", "url": "https://x.com/somarkai/status/2112574994152636502", "text": "Beyond OCR. Meet OXR.\nOnly 1.3B. Open source.\n\n#1 on olmOCR-Bench, OmniDocBench & DocParsingBench🏆\n#1 in parsing speed among open-source models⚡\n\nRSI-powered. A first in document parsing.\nTurn documents into Agent-Friendly data.\n\nIf OXR helps, give us a star on GitHub! 🌟", "name": "SoMark", "handle": "somarkai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2054830841197690880/72QHhpxV_200x200.jpg", "likes": 64, "rts": 15, "replies": 19, "views": 235899, "ts": 1792512103, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112574131791097857/vid/avc1/720x720/sb4cgnPfueTkA0vb.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112574131791097857/vid/avc1/1200x1200/ohWAOZCkHsVrYIVo.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112574131791097857/img/WA95Dj7H23zc6QHc.jpg", "dur": 18}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.03, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112522397362606110", "url": "https://x.com/harshmadhusudan/status/2112522397362606110", "text": "Thank you Dhirubhai and Mukesh Ambani. Thank you to IOCL, HPCL and BPCL etc. Thank you to all engineers who worked on some of the most complex refineries in the world. While the world faces terrible diesel crack spreads, we earn valuable foreign exchange thanks to our refineries.", "name": "Harsh Gupta Madhusudan", "handle": "harshmadhusudan", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1958379378062311424/WSWsCxka_200x200.jpg", "likes": 5408, "rts": 732, "replies": 30, "views": 58219, "ts": 1792499562, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112489145348264263", "url": "https://x.com/siddhantvm/status/2112489145348264263", "text": "MARCO RUBIO : India is a refining superpower", "name": "Siddhant Mishra", "handle": "siddhantvm", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2025076458264444930/LSqUmry9_200x200.jpg", "likes": 369, "rts": 54, "replies": 13, "views": 152475, "ts": 1792491635, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.03, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112614178980843765", "url": "https://x.com/yatharthmann/status/2112614178980843765", "text": "Wow! Elon Musk fired a Muslim just because of his religion! \n\nHe's such an Islamophobe!", "name": "Yatharth Mann", "handle": "yatharthmann", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2041184115131916288/XdogQZvG_200x200.jpg", "likes": 3378, "rts": 326, "replies": 679, "views": 511890, "ts": 1792521445, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112611845320404992/vid/avc1/640x360/6rDvmY6Y033RVFEt.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112611845320404992/vid/avc1/1280x720/firPbz6y4rGxiD8t.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112611845320404992/img/tz7c4BTeEkdPPgao.jpg", "dur": 42}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.03, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112655787961295224", "url": "https://x.com/KanekoaTheGreat/status/2112655787961295224", "text": "ELON MUSK: SpaceX took the team that dominates space and “applied that same team to the deployment of terrestrial compute.”\n\n“This is a bit like the New York Yankees playing in little league. It’s not fair.”\n\nSpaceX puts almost 90% of all mass into orbit. China is roughly 6%. The rest of the world combined, including the rest of the U.S., is about 4%.\n\nThat’s “an order of magnitude greater” than all its space competitors combined.\n\nNow that team is deploying power, cooling, and infrastructure “vastly faster than anyone else, and may at some point be faster than everyone else combined.”\n\n“Let that sink in for a minute.”", "name": "KanekoaTheGreat", "handle": "KanekoaTheGreat", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1612188077333835776/qxjhM55m_200x200.jpg", "likes": 3744, "rts": 382, "replies": 31, "views": 102962, "ts": 1792531365, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112654843756400640/vid/avc1/1280x720/fZYqrNXVnRvVg4-z.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112654843756400640/vid/avc1/1920x1080/xVHUqGrp9hr9xSWf.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112654843756400640/img/WI6lvb6AUmXBYQ14.jpg", "dur": 61}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Sports", "score": 5.03, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112596772099064117", "url": "https://x.com/urdeaintech/status/2112596772099064117", "text": "Re-explaining context every single day gets old fast.\n\n➔ Having local memory on your Mac changes everything. \n\n➔ It quietly handles drafts and notes while you sleep.\n\nGreat approach by @Shogun_AI and @toruai.", "name": "Samuel Urdea", "handle": "urdeaintech", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2092899894218416128/ZypwJ5s7_200x200.jpg", "likes": 28, "rts": 3, "replies": 0, "views": 633, "ts": 1792517295, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112593925114634603", "url": "https://x.com/toruai/status/2112593925114634603", "text": "Your AI forgets you every time you close it. \n\nEvery assistant today works the same way. You open a chat, re-explain your job, get an answer, and start from zero tomorrow.  Smart, sure. Useful? \n\nOnly while you're typing.  It doesn't know about yesterday's meeting. It does nothing until you ask. \n\nAnd most of them want your whole work history on someone else's server to remember it.  \n\nWe built Shogun for exactly this.\n@Shogun_AI_\nShogun is a private, local-first memory on your Mac. It remembers your meetings, drafts, and docs, then works while you sleep: prepares replies, organizes what it can, writes your daily brief.  You wake up, review, approve. \n\nNothing goes out without your yes. Your personal AGI, always running on your computer.\n\nThe first 500 users get a month free.\n\nFollow @Shogun_AI_ @toruai\nand comment 『ShogunAI』", "name": "Toru.T", "handle": "toruai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2077537203614605312/9S3FfAKk_200x200.jpg", "likes": 87, "rts": 44, "replies": 51, "views": 21629, "ts": 1792516616, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112592786579189760/vid/avc1/1280x720/kJpS_CWA4h8yYETb.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112592786579189760/vid/avc1/3840x2160/0kg65h_VD_oWzGWC.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112592786579189760/img/uhPh59whRg063POW.jpg", "dur": 132}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.03, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112569779601178926", "url": "https://x.com/kaif9998/status/2112569779601178926", "text": "an orange box, two pixel eyes and a line for a mouth\n\nthat's the whole face, a Voxel by @roboticscorp has more personality than most apps i've designed\n\nthat's what happens when a robotics team brings in Pixar advisors", "name": "Kaif", "handle": "kaif9998", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2012834364862705664/hWdVyUJE_200x200.jpg", "likes": 16, "rts": 2, "replies": 9, "views": 461, "ts": 1792510859, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/960x720/cMYjra9bu_jYUTYR.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/2880x2160/glhkyiQ6K97Rmq93.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112564839251931136/img/GKLfsqVaQmO0B-kn.jpg", "dur": 89}], "quote": {"id": "2112565146354860151", "url": "https://x.com/make_robot_go/status/2112565146354860151", "text": "Introducing Voxel, a droid butler made by Tuesday Labs.", "name": "Ros Shinkle", "handle": "make_robot_go", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1761551110303825920/JvPQiGQd_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2181, "rts": 228, "replies": 203, "views": 1850860, "ts": 1792509755, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/960x720/cMYjra9bu_jYUTYR.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/2880x2160/glhkyiQ6K97Rmq93.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112564839251931136/img/GKLfsqVaQmO0B-kn.jpg", "dur": 89}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.02, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112569403971981406", "url": "https://x.com/GreylockVC/status/2112569403971981406", "text": "Founders learn to obsess over product-market fit. Greylock Partner @jerrychen says to look just as hard at who should write the first check. He calls it founder-VC fit.\n\nIn 2018, Jerry read a technical blog about M3, an open source project built at Uber, led by engineers Rob Skillington @roskilli and Martin Mao @martin_c_mao. At the time, they hadn’t even decided to start a company.\n\nWhat followed was a five-month courtship.\n\nJerry was trying to convince Martin and Rob to take his investment. As first-time founders, they were diligencing him just as closely.\n\nMartin sent him an 85-page business plan to see who would really do the work, understand the technology, and align with where they wanted to take it.\n\nRob and Martin eventually started @chronosphereio, with M3 as its technical foundation and Jerry wrote the company’s first check.\n\nSeven years later, the company was acquired by @PaloAltoNtwks for $3.35B.  \n\nFor founders, choosing the early investor can shape the company’s trajectory for years. The relationship deserves as much diligence as the financing.\n\nFull story in the comments.", "name": "Greylock Partners", "handle": "GreylockVC", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2076850957607133184/PuYJpvfw_200x200.jpg", "likes": 19, "rts": 3, "replies": 6, "views": 3858, "ts": 1792510770, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112569355091488768/vid/avc1/1280x720/eUce8BZCJXhZoEys.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112569355091488768/vid/avc1/3840x2160/G_RDROx9sNzGSZYU.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFaxmmaYAA2Wr2.jpg", "dur": 49}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.02, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}]);